# 🧭 UI Depth & Hierarchy Rulebook

### Purpose
Guidelines to fix boring UIs, avoid annoying color combos, and create visual depth, hierarchy, and emotional balance.

---

## 1. Foundations — “3D Perception” Framework

### **Z-Space Layers**
| Layer | Purpose | Example |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **Z-0 (Background)** | Canvas base | Neutral `#f8f9fa` / `#0a0a0a` |
| **Z-1 (Surface)** | Cards, containers | Slightly raised `shadow-sm` |
| **Z-2 (Interactive)** | Buttons, inputs | Higher contrast `shadow-md` |
| **Z-3 (Floating)** | Modals, tooltips | Full elevation `shadow-xl` |

> ✅ Keep consistent elevation increments; avoid global heavy shadows.

---

### **Typographic Hierarchy**
| Role | Size | Weight | Example |
|------|------|---------|----------|
| Title / H1 | 28–36px | 700–800 | `text-3xl font-bold` |
| Section Heading | 18–22px | 600 | `text-xl font-semibold` |
| Body | 14–16px | 400–500 | `text-base` |
| Caption | 12px | 400 | `text-xs text-muted-foreground` |

> If the layout works in grayscale, the hierarchy is correct.

---

### **Spacing Rhythm**
Use consistent scales → `4, 8, 16, 24, 32px`

| Element | Padding / Margin |
|----------|------------------|
| Section | 48px top/bottom |
| Card | 24px |
| Item | 12px |
| Icon gap | 8px |

---

## 2. Color System — Fixing Annoying Combos

# Saturation Control
Keep surfaces desaturated (5–10%)
Use vivid color only for actions/highlights
Maintain text contrast > 4.5:1

# Practical Notes
Depth = layering + light. Use shadows, borders, and blurs sparingly.
Hierarchy = contrast + spacing + scale.
Emotion = controlled saturation + rhythm.
TL;DR — Depth through Z-space, clarity through hierarchy, calm through color discipline.

### **Palette Rule (3-1-1)**
- 3 **neutrals** (background, surface, border)
- 1 **primary**
- 1 **accent** *(optional)*

Example:
```js
{
  background: "#0f1115",
  surface: "#1b1e24",
  border: "#2a2d35",
  primary: "#166534",
  accent: "#2dd4bf"
}


/* ----------------------------
   Shadows & Depth (Actual Code)
   ---------------------------- */

.combined {
  /* Layered shadow for realistic depth */
  box-shadow:
    0px 4px 4px #00000030,   /* strong near shadow */
    0px 12px 12px #00000015; /* soft far shadow */
}

.dark {
  /* Deeper contrast shadow */
  box-shadow: 0px 4px 4px #00000030;
}

.light {
  /* Subtle ambient shadow */
  box-shadow: 0px 12px 12px #00000015;
}
